childhood cancer survivors (nephrectomy for renal tumors), nephrectomy treatment, >20 participants, renal function 
assessed >1 year post-treatment.

Study 51: Late effects of intensive treatment for acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplasia in childhood
  Decision: INCLUDE
  Confidence: medium
  Rationale: Study of 33 childhood AML/myelodysplasia survivors. Reports abnormalities of renal function in both 
