Study 59: Impact of drug therapy, radiation dose, and dose rate on renal toxicity following bone marrow transplantation
  Decision: INCLUDE
  Confidence: medium
  Rationale: Retrospective review of 12 articles (1108 patients) evaluating late renal toxicity after TBI/chemotherapy 
conditioning for BMT. Includes pediatric population subgroup. Reports on renal complications related to TBI dose, dose 
rate, and chemotherapy. Meets criteria: includes childhood cancer survivors, radiation involving kidney region, >20 
participants, renal outcomes reported.

Study 62: Renal insufficiency after bone marrow transplantation in children
  Decision: INCLUDE
  Confidence: high
  Rationale: Study of 64 pediatric BMT patients (mean age 7.6 years) with follow-up 2 months to 11 years. Reports on 
