cancer survivors, radiation involving kidney region, >20 participants, renal outcomes reported.

Study 66: Renal size and function after cure of Wilms' tumour
  Decision: INCLUDE
  Confidence: high
  Rationale: Study of 53 Wilms tumor survivors with mean follow-up 13 years. Reports on renal dysfunction (32%), 
including low GFR (19%), hypertension (11%), and increased urinary albumin (9%). Meets criteria: childhood cancer 
survivors, nephrectomy treatment, >20 participants, renal function assessed >1 year post-treatment.

Study 71: Risk factors for long‐term outcome of ifosfamide‐induced nephrotoxicity in children
  Decision: INCLUDE
  Confidence: high
  Rationale: Study of 174 children receiving ifosfamide for various cancers. Assessed at multiple timepoints including 5
years after treatment. Reports on tubular and glomerular dysfunction with multivariable analysis identifying age and 
cumulative dose as risk factors. Meets criteria: childhood cancer survivors, ifosfamide treatment, >20 participants, 
renal function assessed >1 year post-treatment.

Study 73: Long‐term nephrotoxicity in adult survivors of childhood cancer
  Decision: INCLUDE
  Confidence: high
  Rationale: Study of 763 adult survivors of childhood cancer with median follow-up 18.3 years. Reports on eGFR, 
