>20 participants, renal function assessed >1 year post-treatment.

Study 75: Partial reversibility of cisplatin nephrotoxicity in children
  Decision: INCLUDE
  Confidence: high
  Rationale: Study of 40 children assessed at least 18 months (median 2.5 years) after cisplatin treatment cessation. 
Reports on GFR measurements showing partial recovery from cisplatin glomerular toxicity. Meets criteria: childhood 
cancer survivors, cisplatin treatment, >20 participants, renal function assessed >1 year post-treatment.

Study 76: Ifosfamide‐induced nephrotoxicity in 593 sarcoma patients: a report from the Late Effects Surveillance System
  Decision: INCLUDE
  Confidence: high
  Rationale: Prospective study of 593 children/adolescents with sarcoma treated with ifosfamide. Median follow-up 19 
months. Reports on tubulopathy incidence (4.6%) and identifies cumulative dose and young age as risk factors via 
