  ### 3. Additional context (if relevant):                                                                              
  The screening was conducted conservatively per protocol guidelines. Studies were included when they reported renal    
  function outcomes (eGFR, creatinine clearance, proteinuria, tubular markers) in childhood cancer survivors treated    
  with cisplatin, carboplatin, ifosfamide, radiation involving kidneys, or nephrectomy, with follow-up ≥1 year after    
  treatment cessation and n≥20 participants. The included studies span multiple cancer types (Wilms tumor, germ cell    
  tumors, sarcomas, neuroblastoma, lymphomas) and treatment modalities, providing a comprehensive evidence base for     
  evaluating early and late adverse renal effects. Several large cohort studies (CCSS, Kaiser Permanente) were          
  included which will contribute valuable prevalence data. The exclusion of adult-only studies and methodology papers   
  ensures the review focuses specifically on childhood cancer survivorship outcomes." "")                               
